    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d714-a1">

                <pb facs="0706" n="1440" xml:id="pg1440"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 755.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herbert to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith, for
                    your informal ion, a copy of a letter from Rear-Admiral Thomas O. Selfridge,
                    commanding United States naval force on European station, dated the 2d instant,
                    inclosing a translation of a letter written by him to the vali of Aleppo, in
                    regard to the plundering and burning of the American mission station at
                    Marash.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. A. Herbert</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
